<details><summary>Reveal the metric and area definitions</summary>
A tangent vector $(u,v)$ has squared length $u^2/\cosh^2y+\cosh^2x\,v^2$. The area density is $\cosh x/\cosh y$, so region area is obtained by integrating that density against $dx\,dy$.
